@page "/solutions/excel-reconciliation-software"
@{
    var faq = new (string Q, string A)[]
    {
        ("How is this different from Excel's own tools?", "Excel can match two clean columns. Reconza cleans the data first (IDs, dates, amounts), handles several files and one-to-many matches, explains every mismatch, and repeats the same rules every week without anyone rebuilding formulas."),
        ("How is it different from Zapier or Make?", "Those are general automation builders. Reconza is purpose-built for reconciliation: matching, exceptions, review and a settlement report — no pipeline to design."),
        ("Can I define my own reconciliation?", "Yes. Start from a blank workflow: define your fields, add each source file with its role, choose the keys to match on and the amounts to compare."),
    };
}
@section Head {
    @JsonLd.Script(JsonLd.Breadcrumbs(AppUrls, ("Home", "/"), ("Excel reconciliation software", "/solutions/excel-reconciliation-software")))
    @JsonLd.Script(JsonLd.Faq(faq))
}
<section class="page-hero">
    <span class="badge badge-brand">For finance &amp; operations teams</span>
    <h1>Excel reconciliation software for reports that never match</h1>
    <p>Merge and match supplier statements, branch reports and customer files without formulas. Messy headers, different date formats and inconsistent IDs are handled for you.</p>
    <div class="row" style="justify-content:center"><a class="btn btn-lg" href="/tools/compare-excel-files">Compare two files free</a><a class="btn btn-lg btn-secondary" href="/Account/Register">Start free trial</a></div>
</section>
<div class="prose section">
    <h2>Reconciliations people use it for</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Supplier statement vs purchase register</strong> — invoices missing on either side, amount differences.</li>
        <li><strong>Distributor stock or claims reports</strong> — each distributor's format mapped once, compared against your dispatch records.</li>
        <li><strong>Customer remittance vs invoices</strong> — which invoices a payment actually covers, and what was short-paid.</li>
        <li><strong>Branch or warehouse reports</strong> — consolidating files that each branch formats a little differently.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What makes spreadsheets hard to reconcile</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Same ID, different spelling:</strong> <code>INV-0042</code>, <code>inv 42</code>, <code>INV0042</code>. Reconza compares a normalized form.</li>
        <li><strong>Dates:</strong> dd/MM vs MM/dd, text vs real dates, Excel serial numbers — set the format per source once.</li>
        <li><strong>Amounts as text:</strong> currency symbols, Indian digit grouping (1,23,456.00), brackets for negatives.</li>
        <li><strong>Report noise:</strong> title rows above the header, blank rows, totals rows.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>For a quick one-off check, the <a href="/tools/compare-excel-files">free comparison tool</a> needs no account. For anything you do every week or month, set up a workflow and keep the history.</p>
</div>
<section class="section faq">
    <h2 class="section-title">Questions</h2>
    @foreach (var (q, a) in faq) { <details><summary>@q</summary><p>@a</p></details> }
</section>
<partial name="_Cta" model="@((string?)null)" />
